11
00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:54.630
Well, in this context, it means to give a defense, give some kind of

12
00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:59.490
defending idea of what it means to, uh, about what you believe.

13
00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:04.950
This is actually the Greek word apologia.

14
00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.910
And that's where we get the idea of apologetics.

15
00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:10.890
It literally comes from the word apology.

16
00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:16.050
Now we're not talking about I'm apologizing for what I believe, but if you can

17
00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:21.150
imagine for a moment, a courtroom scenario where you were on the stand and you had

18
00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:25.650
to give sort of a defense. You had to give a reason for your actions, a reason for

19
00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:28.850
what you believe, or a reason just for what you're doing.

20
00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:33.710
Well in the ancient world, in the context that Peter is talking about here, is to a

21
00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:36.530
bunch of Christians who are being persecuted by the Roman government.

22
00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:42.690
Now here, Peter's telling the believers to be prepared,

23
00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:48.250
to know why you believe what you believe, to be able to stand in a formal sense

24
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:53.990
in this context, to give a reason, to give a defense, to defend one's belief

